{# Report page chrome (S8, 2026-09-04).

   The fifteen detail reports were the same page fifteen times: a
   2.75rem title, a paragraph of prose, a "Save view / All reports"
   pair, then a second row holding the range picker, then a third row
   (.report-toolbar) holding the search box, the row count and the
   export kebab. Three bands of chrome before the first number.

   This macro is all three, merged into the one .app-toolbar strip
   described in docs/app-chrome-guide.md. It is a macro rather than
   fifteen hand-edits so the strip cannot drift page to page.

   The page's own filters come through {% call %}; everything else is
   a parameter, because Nunjucks gives a macro exactly one caller.

     {% from "partials/report-chrome.njk" import reportChrome %}
     {% call reportChrome(
          title="Spending by category",
          id="spending",
          info="<p>Outflows by category.</p>",
          infoTitle="About this report",
          save="Save this range as a view.",
          slug="spending-by-category",
          searchId="sp-search",
          searchPlaceholder="Filter by group or category",
          count='<span x-text="visibleCount"></span> rows') %}
       ...the page's range controls...
     {% endcall %}

   Arguments
     title     the screen-reader <h1>. The page name, unchanged.
     id        unique on the page; ids the info modal.
     info      the old .app-page__lead, raw HTML, shown in the modal.
               Never delete the words -- they are the only explanation
               the report has.
     save      tooltip for the "Save this view" item in the actions
               kebab. Empty means the page has no saved views and the
               item is not rendered. It is a menu item rather than a
               button because Save view + All reports side by side put
               the actions on a second row at 1024.
     slug/csv  passed straight to reportExports.
     searchId  renders the table search box in the strip. Empty means
               the report has no searchable table.
     count     raw HTML for the row count that used to sit in
               .report-toolbar.
     context   raw HTML for a range label, for a page whose date
               pickers live in the collapsed filter row and would
               otherwise leave the reader guessing what window they
               are looking at.
     filtersId id of an .app-filters row under the strip; renders the
               Filters toggle and its count badge. The badge is not
               optional: a filter that is on and hidden is a reader
               staring at a short list wondering where the rows went.
#}
{% macro reportChrome(title, id, info, infoTitle="", infoLabel="", save="", slug="", csv="",
                      searchId="", searchPlaceholder="", searchLabel="Filter",
                      count="", context="", filtersId="") %}
{% from "partials/report-exports.njk" import reportExports %}
{% from "partials/page-info.njk" import pageInfo %}
<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ title }}</h1>
<div class="app-toolbar report-chrome">
  <div class="app-toolbar__group">
    {{ caller() }}
    {% if filtersId %}
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost app-toolbar__filter-toggle"
            @click="filtersOpen = !filtersOpen"
            :aria-expanded="filtersOpen.toString()"
            aria-controls="{{ filtersId }}">
      Filters
      <span class="app-toolbar__filter-count" x-show="activeFilterCount()" x-cloak
            x-text="activeFilterCount()"></span>
    </button>
    {% endif %}
    {% if searchId %}
    <div class="field report-chrome__search">
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="{{ searchId }}">{{ searchLabel }}</label>
      <input class="input" id="{{ searchId }}" type="search" x-model="query"
             placeholder="{{ searchPlaceholder }}">
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if context %}<span class="app-toolbar__context">{{ context | safe }}</span>{% endif %}
    {% if count %}<span class="app-toolbar__context report-chrome__count">{{ count | safe }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="app-toolbar__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/app/reports/">All reports</a>
    {{ reportExports(slug, csv, save) }}
    {% call pageInfo(id=id, title=infoTitle or ("About " + title), label=infoLabel or ("What " + title + " shows")) %}
      {{ info | safe }}
    {% endcall %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
